// ProjectList: fetchProjects().then(setProjects)  -> useState copy
// ProjectDetail: fetchProject(id).then(setProject) -> useState copy
// renameProject(id, name): updates server + detail page's local copy only

Tickets: 31 reports/quarter, tag "rename-ghost". List stale until F5.
Project data is owned by the ___b1___, so each useState copy is an unkeyed
fork that no mutation can find and ___b2___. The fix: read through a query
cache keyed per resource, and make the rename mutation ___b2___ the affected
keys — every subscriber refetches. Local useState remains correct only for
___b3___ state the UI itself owns.

